# What never belongs in the image.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` copied the entire working tree, including
# everything git ignores, and the served image was 19.3GB. The application is
# a Python API; almost none of that was it.
#
# Written as an allowlist of exclusions rather than `*` plus re-inclusions,
# because a deny-by-default list silently drops a new source directory the day
# somebody adds one, and the failure appears at runtime as a missing module.

# Local environments and caches — the image installs its own dependencies.
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Lean build output. The proofs are source and are not run in the image; the
# `.lake` directory alone is gigabytes of compiled artefacts.
formal/.lake/

# History and tooling. `.git` is tens of megabytes and the image needs none of
# it — the deployment identity arrives as an environment variable, not from a
# working tree.
.git/
.github/
.aider*

# Infrastructure. Terraform state, plans and Ansible roles describe how the
# image is deployed; shipping them inside it is circular.
infra/

# Local data. Snapshots, databases and generated reports are mounted or
# fetched at runtime, never baked in.
data/cache/
data/history/
data/models/
data/snapshots/
data/*.db
reports/
evidence/

# Test surfaces and corpora. The image serves; it does not measure itself.
tests/
corpus/parser/parses.json
corpus/parser/hosted.json
